SECRETS

- (secrets) gives an alist of (key . description); values hidden.
- (secret "REPL_TOKEN") gives the value as a tainted string. It behaves like a
  string in all string functions and taint propagates through the result, but it
  prints redacted as a hash-and-angle-brackets printout naming only the key, and
  is only revealed when serialized into an outgoing MCP call argument or header.
  Only REPL_-prefixed keys are visible.
  Example: (load-mcp :name "acme" :url "…" :headers (list (cons "Authorization" (secret "REPL_ACME_TOKEN")))).

The string built-ins are taint-aware: taint flows through every result computed
from a secret.

GOTCHAS

- A secret prints as a hash-and-angle-brackets printout naming only its key. That
  printout cannot be read back, so typing one into a form is always an error —
  call (secret "KEY") again, or use the name you bound it to.
